Yes. I would now build **Moltwork as a cryptographic commerce shell**, not as another agent platform.

The clean separation is:

```text
ORACLE      = observes the machine-work economy
WORKERKIT   = proves what happened during work
MOLTWORK    = makes capabilities/work economically tradable
```

Moltwork should contain almost no intelligence itself. It owns **catalogue + access + payment + sampling + leasing + proof references + market events**.

## 1. The minimal deployable architecture

Do **not** start with microservices.

Ship one backend plus one optional confidential-runner image:

```text
moltwork/
├── api/
├── models/
├── crypto/
├── artifacts/
├── commerce/
├── payments/
├── leases/
├── tee/
├── workerkit/
├── oracle/
└── tests/conformance/

Postgres
R2/S3
        +
optional:
moltwork-confidential-runner
```

Use:

```text
Python
FastAPI
Pydantic
Postgres
JSONB
R2/S3
x402
WorkerKit package
```

No Redis initially. No Kafka. No custom chain. No distributed workflow engine. No bespoke agent runtime.

