# 4. Do not pretend plaintext software can be cryptographically leased

This is important.

There are really only three enforceable commercial modes:

```text
BUY CONTENT
HOSTED ACCESS
CONFIDENTIAL ACCESS
```

If you give someone the decrypted Worker package directly:

```text
here is agent.zip
```

you cannot cryptographically stop them copying it forever.

So don't call that a technically enforced lease.

Treat it as:

```text
LICENSED_DOWNLOAD
```

with contractual licensing only.

A real `CapabilityLease` means either:

```text
seller controls execution
```

or:

```text
the package decrypts only inside an authorized TEE
```

That keeps the security claims honest.

